# docker bind-mount data (postgres / pgadmin)
data/


# Standalone clone of the MCP server (chungweeeei/SyncAI-ROS-MCP), if anyone keeps
# one here as a local scratch copy. It is a different repository's working tree and
# must never be committed into this one; the vendored in-tree copy it used to
# shadow (src/syncai_ros_mcp) was removed, and lives in git history now.
src/syncai-ros-mcp/

# Materialised by `vcs import < third-party.repos`, not committed -- six upstream
# repos, each with its own .git, which is why this rule matters more than it
# looks: without it a `git add -A` stages all six as gitlinks with no .gitmodules
# behind them, and a fresh clone gets six empty directories. `gitkeep` is
# negated so the directory itself survives a clone and vcs has somewhere to
# import into.
src/third-party/*
!src/third-party/gitkeep

# Same arrangement for a standalone clone of the backend (chungweeeei/
# SyncAI-Robot-Backend), if anyone keeps one here to develop it against the ROS
# interfaces. It is a different repository's working tree and must never be
# committed into this one; it was 120 tracked files here until the 2026-09
# split, which git history still has. Note colcon WILL pick a clone up and
# build it — that is the point of putting it here rather than beside the
# workspace, but it also means `colcon build` failures from it are not this
# repo's.
src/syncai_backend/

# LIO map output (pcd / gridmap / poses — regenerated, not tracked).
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `map/` matches a directory of that name
# at any depth, and it was silently swallowing a `repositories/map/` package
# directory inside what is now SyncAI-Robot-Backend. Files already tracked
# there stayed visible, so nothing looked wrong until a new module in it went
# missing from a commit.
/map/

# TTS model weights (kokoro-onnx: kokoro-v1.0.onnx + voices-v1.0.bin, ~330 MB).
# Nothing in this workspace downloads or reads them any more — TTS left with
# the backend in 2026-09 — but robots that ran the in-tree backend still have
# the directory, and the rule is what keeps it out of a commit. Anchored for
# the same reason as /map/ above: a bare `models/` would swallow any future
# src/**/models/ package directory.
/models/

# Hand-recorded rosbags (record/<name>/*.db3 + metadata.yaml, written by
# `ros2 bag record` in a shell; the REST route that also wrote here went with
# the backend). Anchored with a leading slash for the reason /map/ and /models/
# above give: a bare `record/` matches a directory of that name at any depth,
# and would silently swallow a future src/**/record/ package directory.
/record/

# Materialised by `vcs import < interface.repos`, not committed -- the same
# arrangement src/third-party/ has. It was 28 tracked files in this repo until
# the 2026-09 split moved it to SyncAI-Robot-Interface, so that the backend
# could build against the interfaces without checking out the whole workspace.
# Edit the messages THERE; a change made in this directory is untracked and the
# next --force import overwrites it.
src/syncai_common/
